    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-11-18T21:17:59+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-18T21:17:59+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-18T10:47:59Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-18T10:47:59Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A low pressure system and associated trough over Western Australia move over western South Australia this evening and broadly across the state during Thursday, clearing to the east early Friday. A high pressure system will then move across southern SA from Friday, before a trough and cold front move across the west late Saturday and across the rest of SA on Sunday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW014" description="North East Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-11-18T21:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-19T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-18T10:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-18T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower west of Leigh Creek, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Leigh Creek. Winds east to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-19T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-20T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-18T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-19T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers, most likely from the late morning. A thunderstorm likely, possibly severe with damaging winds, large hail and heavy rain which may lead to flash flooding west of Leigh Creek. Winds northeast to southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h tending northwest to northeasterly 25 to 40 km/h in the early morning. Overnight temperatures falling to 21 to 27 with daytime temperatures reaching the mid to high 30s.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">High</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 8:50am to 5:00pm, UV Index predicted to reach 11 [Extreme]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-20T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-21T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-19T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-20T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower east of Leigh Creek, most likely in the early morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the morning and afternoon, possibly severe with damaging winds, large hail and heavy rain which may lead to flash flooding in the far northeast. Winds northwest to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending northwest to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h in the morning then tending south to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 18 and 25 with daytime temperatures reaching the mid to high 30s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-21T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-22T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-20T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-21T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny. Winds southeast to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h tending northeast to southeasterly during the morning then tending northwest to northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 16 and 25 with daytime temperatures reaching 35 to 40.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-11-22T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-23T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-21T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-22T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Medium chance of showers south of Yunta in the morning and afternoon. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of raised dust north of Leigh Creek in the morning. The chance of a thunderstorm east of Leigh Creek in the afternoon and evening. Winds northwest to northeasterly 30 to 45 km/h tending northwest to southwesterly during the day then tending south to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to 21 to 28 with daytime temperatures reaching 39 to 45.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
